<title>ITALY: Italy's Omnitel sees operating breakeven in 1997. [CORRECTED 13:40 GMT]</title>
<headline>Italy's Omnitel sees operating breakeven in 1997. [CORRECTED 13:40 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's second mobile phone operator Omnitel, should breakeven in 1997 at the operating level, before interest payments and taxes, the managing director of the company, Silvio Scaglia, said.</p>
<p>Olivetti is the largest shareholder in the group with a stake of 35.5 percent.</p>
<p>(Corrects size of stake from &quot;just over 40 percent&quot; to &quot;35.5 percent&quot;)</p>
<p>Scaglia confirmed Omnitel's goal of a general breakeven in 1998. He added that the company had 1.71 million clients at the end of last year.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
